  "result": "Perfect! All 180 tests pass (171 original + 9 new voucher tests). Here's what I implemented:\n\n\u2705 **Added `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` function to `src/invoices.js`**\n- Applies a fixed-amount voucher to an invoice\n- Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n- Voucher reduces total after VAT: total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher\n- Never mutates the invoice argument\n\n\u2705 **Enforced constraints:**\n- **NOT_DRAFT**: Only draft invoices can have vouchers applied\n- **VOUCHER_EXISTS**: Only one voucher per invoice\n- **AMOUNT_INVALID**: Amount must be a positive integer (in cents)\n\n\u2705 **Updated `invoiceTotals(invoice)`** to include voucher calculation\n- Returns new field `voucher` (0 if no voucher applied)\n- New total formula: subtotal - discount + vat - voucher\n- All amounts clamped at 0\n\n\u2705 **Added `VOUCHER_EXISTS` error** to `src/errors.js`\n\n\u2705 **Comprehensive tests** (9 new) covering:\n- Applying voucher to draft invoice\n- VOUCHER_EXISTS error when voucher already present\n- NOT_DRAFT error on non-draft invoices\n- AMOUNT_INVALID errors (zero, negative, float)\n- `invoiceTotals` calculations with and without vouchers\n- Immutability of invoice objects\n\n\u2705 **Updated existing tests** to include voucher field in invoiceTotals expectations",
